t highlight it and=0A                                                    se=
lect Remove.&lt;/p&gt;=0A=0A=0A=0A=0A=0A                                         =
       &lt;h3 class=3D&quot;my-4&quot;&gt;Setup a New Printer (Mac)&lt;/h3&gt;=0A=0A             =
                                   &lt;strong&gt;=0A                             =
                       1.Prepare your printer:=0A                          =
                      &lt;/strong&gt;=0A=0A                                      =
          &lt;p&gt;Use the instructions that came with your printer to=0A        =
                                            unpack the printer, install ink=
 or toner, and add paper.=0A                                               =
     Turn on the printer and make sure it=E2=80=99s not displaying=0A      =
                                              any errors.&lt;/p&gt;=0A=0A        =
                                        &lt;strong&gt;=0A                        =
                            2. Connect your printer: Follow the instruction=
s that=0A                                                    came with the =
printer to connect it to the network.=0A                                   =
             &lt;/strong&gt;=0A=0A                                               =
 &lt;p&gt;=0A                                                    If you have a Wi=
-Fi printer, you might need to connect=0A                                  =
                  the printer to your Mac with a USB cable to set up Wi-Fi=
=0A                                                    printing. After conn=
ecting the printer to your Mac,=0A                                         =
           install the Mac software that came with the printer and=0A      =
                                              use the printer=E2=80=99s set=
up assistant to connect the printer=0A                                     =
               to your Wi-Fi network. After setting up, you can=0A         =
                                           disconnect the cable from your p=
rinter and Mac and the=0A                                                  =
  printer should remain connected to the Wi-Fi network.=0A                 =
                               &lt;/p&gt;=0A=0A                                  =
              &lt;strong&gt;=0A                                                  =
  3. Add the printer to your list of available printers:=0A                =
                                &lt;/strong&gt;=0A=0A                            =
                    &lt;p&gt;=0A                                                 =
   Choose Apple menu &gt; System Settings, then click Printers=0A             =
                                       &amp; Scanners in the sidebar. (You may =
need to scroll=0A                                                    down.)=
&lt;/p&gt;=0A=0A                                                &lt;strong&gt;=0A      =
                                              4. When your printer appears =
in the list, select your=0A                                                =
    printer, then click Add.=0A                                            =
    &lt;/strong&gt;=0A=0A=0A                                                &lt;p&gt; I=
t may take a minute or two for your printer to appear.=0A                  =
                                  If you see a message prompting you to dow=
nload new=0A                                                    software, m=
ake sure to download and install it.&lt;/p&gt;=0A=0A=0A                          =
